+Build the same `helm system-info` command as a Wasm plugin using the [Extism](https://extism.org/) PDK.
+
+### 1. Set up repository
+
+Scaffold a new repository from the template (or just clone):
+https://github.com/gjenkins8/helm-extism-plugin-template
+
+### 2. Update plugin manifest
+
+Note the `runtime` and `runtimeConfig` field values change for Wasm:
+
+```yaml title="plugin.yaml" showLineNumbers
+apiVersion: v1
+type: cli/v1
+name: "system-info"
+version: "0.1.0"
+runtime: extism/v1
+config:
+  usage: system-info
+  shortHelp: Display system and Helm information
+  longHelp: Shows OS info, Helm version, and environment details
+runtimeConfig:
+  memory:
+    maxPages: 16
+  timeout: 30000
+```
+
+### 3. Update `main.go`
+
+Specify the plugin's input/output messages and implement the entry function. The default entry function name is `helm_plugin_main` (configurable via `runtimeConfig.entryFuncName`):
+
+```go title="main.go" showLineNumbers
+package main
+
+...
+
+type InputMessage struct {
+	Args []string `json:"args"`
+}
+
+type OutputMessage struct {
+	Output string `json:"output"`
+}
+
+func systemInfo(input InputMessage) (*OutputMessage, error) {
+	pdk.Log(pdk.LogLevelInfo, "system-info plugin running")
+	output := OutputMessage{
+		Output: fmt.Sprintf("Arguments: %v", input.Args),
+	}
+	return &output, nil
+}
+```
+
+### 4. Build WebAssembly
+
+```bash
+$ make build
+$ ls -la plugin.wasm
+```
+
+### 5. Install in Dev Mode and Test
+
+Same as the Subprocess CLI Plugin step:
+
+```bash
+% helm plugin install $HOME/code/helm/plugins/system-info
+Installing plugin from local directory (development mode)
+Installed plugin: system-info
+
+% helm system-info
+```
+
+What you built: A CLI plugin using the Wasm runtime with sandboxed execution and structured communication via the Extism PDK!
