+Build the same label-injecting postrenderer as a Wasm plugin using the [Extism](https://extism.org/) PDK.
+
+### 1. Set up repository
+
+Scaffold a new repository from the template (or just clone):
+https://github.com/gjenkins8/helm-extism-plugin-template
+
+### 2. Update plugin manifest
+
+Note the `runtime` and `runtimeConfig` field values change for Wasm:
+
+```yaml title="plugin.yaml" showLineNumbers
+apiVersion: v1
+type: postrenderer/v1
+name: label-injector
+version: 0.1.0
+runtime: extism/v1
+runtimeConfig:
+  memory:
+    maxPages: 16
+  timeout: 30000
+```
+
+### 3. Update `main.go`
+
+Specify the plugin's input/output messages. Postrenderer plugins receive the rendered manifests and return the modified manifests:
+
+```go title="main.go" showLineNumbers
+package main
+
+...
+
+type InputMessage struct {
+	Manifests string `json:"manifests"`
+}
+
+type OutputMessage struct {
+	Manifests string `json:"manifests"`
+}
+
+func injectLabels(input InputMessage) (*OutputMessage, error) {
+	// Parse the YAML manifests, add the label, and re-serialize.
+	// See the Subprocess tutorial for the equivalent yq expression.
+	output := OutputMessage{Manifests: input.Manifests}
+	return &output, nil
+}
+```
+
+### 4. Build WebAssembly
+
+```bash
+$ make build
+$ ls -la plugin.wasm
+```
+
+### 5. Install in Dev Mode and Test
+
+Same as the Subprocess Postrenderer step:
+
+```bash
+% helm plugin install $HOME/code/helm/plugins/label-injector
+Installing plugin from local directory (development mode)
+Installed plugin: label-injector
+
+% helm template ../mychart --post-renderer label-injector
+```
+
+What you built: A Postrenderer plugin using the Wasm runtime with sandboxed execution and structured communication via the Extism PDK!
