 Starting with Helm 4, the plugin system is set up to more easily allow adding additional plugin types, which would allow users to modify other areas of Helm functionality.
 
+Helm 4 plugins run on one of two runtimes: the legacy **subprocess** runtime, or the sandboxed **Wasm** runtime (via [Extism](https://extism.org/)). Wasm plugins run in a secure sandbox with only the access to your system that you explicitly approve through `plugin.yaml`. See [Plugin Runtimes](#plugin-runtimes) for details.
+
