+## Migrating from Legacy Plugins
+
+Helm 3 plugins (those without an `apiVersion` field in `plugin.yaml`) are still supported throughout the life of Helm 4, so your existing plugins will continue to work until Helm 5. However, legacy plugins use the subprocess runtime and do not benefit from the Wasm sandbox or the new versioned plugin types.
+
+To migrate a legacy plugin:
+
+1. Check whether the plugin author has published a Helm 4 version of the plugin. If so, uninstall the legacy plugin and install the new version.
+2. If no updated version exists, ask the plugin author to migrate. The [Plugins Developer Guide](/plugins/developer/index.mdx) covers the new `plugin.yaml` fields and the Wasm runtime.
+3. Legacy plugins that use the old downloader mechanism (`protocolCommands`) should be replaced with `getter/v1` plugins, which implement protocol-specific logic by inspecting the download URL.
+
+You can identify legacy plugins in `helm plugin list` by their missing API version.
+
 ## Listing Installed Plugins
 
 The command to list plugins includes the plugin's name, version, type, API version, provenance, and source.
